Root cause:
The functions `vmw_translate_mob_ptr` and `vmw_translate_guest_ptr` were updated to use `vmw_user_bo_lookup`, which returns an error code and sets an output pointer only on success. However, the error path was not updated accordingly and continued to return `PTR_ERR(vmw_bo)` using an uninitialized pointer on failure. This could lead to returning success (0) instead of the actual error code, causing subsequent uninitialized and out-of-bounds accesses.

